tilo-default.bpf is compiled at runtime from the in-tree filter in
src/seccomp.rs (compile_baseline). It is intentionally not checked
in: the BPF blob is host-arch-specific, and shipping a stale or
mismatched blob would silently disable the policy.

If you need a static blob (e.g. to inspect the filter without
linking seccompiler), generate it on the target host with:

    cargo run -p tilo-launcher --bin tilo-launcher --features dump-seccomp -- \
        --dump-seccomp > tilo-launcher/share/tilo-default.bpf
